import{_ as t,o as a,c as n,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const c=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 729 | Critique of Hang-Up Retirement · Overview — The Common Malady of Web-Novel Heavenly Emperors and Immortal Sovereigns","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 729 | Critique of Hang-Up Retirement · Overview — The Common Malady of Web-Novel Heavenly Emperors and Immortal Sovereigns","no":729,"module":4,"tags":["Hang-Up Retirement","Overview","Heavenly Emperor Immortal Sovereign","Common Malady","Protagonist-Uniqueness Dependency"],"related":["04-Anti-Predation Core Treatise","17-Plane-Transcendent Strong-One Standards","90-Glossary"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0729_模块4-挂机养老批判总论.md","filePath":"en/0729_模块4-挂机养老批判总论.md"}'),i={name:"en/0729_模块4-挂机养老批判总论.md"};function r(s,e,l,h,u,d){return a(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-729-critique-of-hang-up-retirement-·-overview-—-the-common-malady-of-web-novel-heavenly-emperors-and-immortal-sovereigns" tabindex="-1">Entry 729 | Critique of Hang-Up Retirement · Overview — The Common Malady of Web-Novel Heavenly Emperors and Immortal Sovereigns <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-729-critique-of-hang-up-retirement-·-overview-—-the-common-malady-of-web-novel-heavenly-emperors-and-immortal-sovereigns" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 729 | Critique of Hang-Up Retirement · Overview — The Common Malady of Web-Novel Heavenly Emperors and Immortal Sovereigns&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 4 · Transcendence Orthodox Definition Library | Benchmark base: Documents 04, 17, 90</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-a-common-ending-a-common-malady" tabindex="-1">Introduction: a common ending, a common malady <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-a-common-ending-a-common-malady" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: a common ending, a common malady&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The last five entries of Module 4 will land critique on concrete IPs. But before critiquing Ye Fan, Shi Hao, Tang San, and Goku, we must first make clear the common traits of this &quot;hang-up retirement&quot; malady — why do all the Heavenly Emperors, Immortal Sovereigns, and cosmic overlords across the web-novel multiverse end up with the same disease? This is not one author&#39;s problem; this is the entire web-novel paradigm&#39;s structural problem.</p><p>Six top-level axioms simultaneously act as the critique&#39;s ruler in this entry: the anti-predation axiom points out these &quot;Heavenly Emperors and Immortal Sovereigns&quot;&#39; power sources are generally unclean; the republican axiom of Myriad Races asks on what basis they monopolize the highest realm; the collective ascension axiom points out they do not carry Myriad Ranks; the causal self-discipline axiom points out their cross-plane operations are never reported; the law-first axiom points out their systems generally eat their own books and end in failure.</p><p>The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-four-symptoms-of-the-common-malady" tabindex="-1">I. Four Symptoms of the Common Malady <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-four-symptoms-of-the-common-malady" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Four Symptoms of the Common Malady&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Dissecting the endings of the four major IPs — Shrouding the Heavens, Perfect World, Douluo, Dragon Ball — the &quot;Heavenly Emperor / Immortal Sovereign disease&quot; has four common symptoms:</p><h3 id="_1-1-the-endpoint-is-the-endpoint" tabindex="-1">1.1 The Endpoint Is the Endpoint <a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-1-the-endpoint-is-the-endpoint" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;1.1 The Endpoint Is the Endpoint&quot;">​</a></h3><p>After the protagonist reaches the summit, the story ends. He has no next step; he does not need one. His &quot;transcendence&quot; is a period, not a comma.</p><h3 id="_1-2-myriad-ranks-stay-where-they-are" tabindex="-1">1.2 Myriad Ranks Stay Where They Are <a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-2-myriad-ranks-stay-where-they-are" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;1.2 Myriad Ranks Stay Where They Are&quot;">​</a></h3><p>After the protagonist ascends, the civilization behind him keeps running, but no longer progresses because of him. He is civilization&#39;s highest point, also civilization&#39;s ceiling — later generations only need to look up; no need to catch up.</p><h3 id="_1-3-knowledge-privatized" tabindex="-1">1.3 Knowledge Privatized <a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-3-knowledge-privatized" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;1.3 Knowledge Privatized&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The protagonist&#39;s manuals, experience, and law understanding are either passed only to bloodline disciples, or vanish with his ascension. No public sharing; no Selfless Dao.</p><h3 id="_1-4-lonely-invincibility" tabindex="-1">1.4 Lonely Invincibility <a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-4-lonely-invincibility" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;1.4 Lonely Invincibility&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The protagonist&#39;s final state is &quot;invincible, immortal, lonely.&quot; He is not symbiotic with Myriad Ranks; he stands above Myriad Ranks. This loneliness is romanticized; readers take it as a strong one&#39;s medal.</p><p>Four symptoms together are &quot;hang-up retirement&quot; — <strong>he has already hung up at the cosmos&#39;s highest point, producing no civilizational increment.</strong></p><h2 id="ii-why-this-malady-is-structural" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Malady Is Structural <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-malady-is-structural" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Malady Is Structural&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This malady is not one author writing off the rails; it is the web-novel paradigm&#39;s inevitable product:</p><ul><li><strong>爽文 logic</strong>: readers want the rush of &quot;the protagonist grows stronger,&quot; not the labor-sense of &quot;the protagonist works.&quot; Once the author writes the protagonist invincible, the story&#39;s thrill point is exhausted;</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness</strong>: the entire civilization revolves around the protagonist; the protagonist stops, the whole story stops. Protagonist-uniqueness-dependency ratings are generally &quot;medium&quot; to &quot;extreme&quot;;</li><li><strong>No post concept</strong>: old web novels have no &quot;transcended-one post&quot; setting; strong ones have nothing to do after reaching the summit, so they can only hang up;</li><li><strong>No Myriad-Rank perspective</strong>: the story is told from the protagonist&#39;s view; Myriad Ranks are only backdrop. The author has no motivation to describe &quot;what happened to Myriad Ranks after the protagonist reached the summit.&quot;</li></ul><p>Four structural reasons together: &quot;hang-up retirement&quot; is not a bug; it is a feature — it is this paradigm&#39;s inevitable ending.</p><h2 id="iii-the-three-layer-harm-of-hang-up-retirement" tabindex="-1">III. The Three-Layer Harm of Hang-Up Retirement <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-the-three-layer-harm-of-hang-up-retirement" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. The Three-Layer Harm of Hang-Up Retirement&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Hang-up retirement looks harmless — the protagonist is already invincible; what&#39;s wrong with letting him rest? Actually it has three layers of harm:</p><h3 id="_3-1-waste-of-civilizational-increments" tabindex="-1">3.1 Waste of Civilizational Increments <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-1-waste-of-civilizational-increments" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.1 Waste of Civilizational Increments&quot;">​</a></h3><p>All of the protagonist&#39;s lifelong cultivation&#39;s computable power, law understanding, and civilizational influence stop producing at the moment he reaches the summit. This is cosmos-grade energy waste.</p><h3 id="_3-2-a-ceiling-for-later-generations" tabindex="-1">3.2 A Ceiling for Later Generations <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-2-a-ceiling-for-later-generations" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.2 A Ceiling for Later Generations&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The protagonist is too strong, too invincible, too lonely; later generations dare not chase, cannot catch up, need not chase. Civilization&#39;s evolution speed is locked by the protagonist personally.</p><h3 id="_3-3-pollution-of-readers-values" tabindex="-1">3.3 Pollution of Readers&#39; Values <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-3-pollution-of-readers-values" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.3 Pollution of Readers&#39; Values&quot;">​</a></h3><p>After readers finish this kind of ending, they form a subconscious: <strong>cultivating is for the day when you may not work.</strong> This value seeping into reality is one of the cultural roots of &quot;lying flat is justice.&quot; Heng Yuan Zhou Library&#39;s Module 4 opposes this value at the law level.</p><h2 id="iv-heng-yuan-zhou-s-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-heng-yuan-zhou-s-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s alternative to &quot;Heavenly Emperor / Immortal Sovereign disease&quot; is everything discussed in the previous 28 entries:</p><ul><li>Change &quot;endpoint&quot; to &quot;post&quot; — the Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm is a permanent-post realm;</li><li>Change &quot;Myriad Ranks stay where they are&quot; to &quot;carry Myriad Ranks along&quot; — the collective ascension axiom;</li><li>Change &quot;knowledge privatized&quot; to &quot;Selfless-Dao public library&quot; — the anti-predation axiom;</li><li>Change &quot;lonely invincibility&quot; to &quot;nine-post symbiosis&quot; — the republican axiom of Myriad Races.</li></ul><p>The next four entries (730–733) will use this alternative to measure Ye Fan, Shi Hao, Tang San, and Goku one by one.</p><h2 id="v-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">V. Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: hang-up retirement is civilization-grade energy waste; Heng Yuan Zhou uproots it with perpetual construction</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: hang-uppers&#39; power sources are generally unclean; old web novels do not audit; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s source audit cuts it from the root</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo and Gu Chensha are representatives of &quot;extreme&quot; protagonist-uniqueness dependency; hang-up retirement is this dependency&#39;s inevitable ending</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: 99% of clans behind the hang-upper are forgotten; Heng Yuan Zhou writes these 99% into the axioms</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: the hang-upper&#39;s manuals vanish with him; Heng Yuan Zhou uses the Selfless Dao to keep knowledge flowing forever</li><li><strong>Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law</strong>: all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity — infinite origin inherent in all; predation naturally loses its meaning</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Heavenly Emperor / Immortal Sovereign disease is not an individual author&#39;s problem; it is the entire web-novel paradigm&#39;s structural problem. Its symptoms are endpoint-is-endpoint, Myriad Ranks stay put, knowledge privatized, lonely invincibility. What Heng Yuan Zhou Library must do is tell all cultivators at the law level: <strong>this is not a strong one&#39;s romance; this is a civilization&#39;s tragedy.</strong></p><p>Understand this malady&#39;s structural nature, and you understand why the next four entries&#39; critique is not aimed at one character — Ye Fan, Shi Hao, Tang San, and Goku are all good characters; their tragedy is imposed on them by the paradigm. What Heng Yuan Zhou must do is not negate these characters, but give them (and the billions of readers behind them) a new option: <strong>after growing strong, you need not hang up; after reaching the summit, you need not be lonely; after becoming invincible, you need not have no target.</strong> The next four entries, one by one.</p><p>In the end, the hang-up-retirement critique overview described in this entry is no isolated case — its causal and energetic traces are throughout filed in the Alaya Network, traceable and correctable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/04-反掠夺主义核心论纲.html">Entry 04 · Anti-Predation Core Treatise</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/17-位面至高强者标准.html">Entry 17 · Plane-Transcendent Strong-One Standards</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/90-术语词典.html">Entry 90 · Glossary</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/703-超脱不是躺平.html">Entry 703 · Transcendence Is Not Lying Flat</a></li></ul>',41)])])}const p=t(i,[["render",r]]);export{c as __pageData,p as default};
